        <headline>Flood Advisory issued September 26 at 5:06AM CDT until September 26 at 1:00PM CDT by NWS Hastings NE</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...Central Jewell County in north central Kansas...
Northwestern Mitchell County in north central Kansas...
Northeastern Osborne County in north central Kansas...
Southeastern Smith County in north central Kansas...

* WHEN...Until 100 PM CDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.
River or stream flows are elevated.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 504 AM CDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated
heavy rain due to thunderstorms. Between 2.5 and 4.5 inches of
rain have fallen.
- Flooding impacts will continue, but no additional rainfall is
expected.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Osborne, Downs, Mankato, Cawker City, Glen Elder, Jewell, Burr
Oak, Ionia, Webber, Montrose and Lovewell State Park.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
